# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# REFERENCE LIBRARY — COPYRIGHTED. MUST NEVER ENTER GIT HISTORY.
#
# HANDOFF G1: the PDFs/DOCXs in this tree are IEEE papers, PhD theses, Intel
# and Xilinx application notes, and the professor's own handwritten notes. In
# the previous checkout they were committed to the baseline commit, which is
# why that repo can never be made public without rewriting history. This
# checkout was `git init`-ed fresh (2026-08-05) specifically so they are
# excluded from commit #1 onward and there is nothing to strip later.
#
# `git status --ignored` and `git ls-files '*.pdf'` are the two checks.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
*.pdf
*.docx
*.doc
*.pptx
resources/

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# PDK — SKY130.
#
# The working install lives OUT OF TREE at C:\Users\DELL\sky130A (HANDOFF G33),
# so nothing here should match today. These patterns exist so that a PDK copied
# or symlinked into the repo (~52 MB, 856 files, and not ours to redistribute)
# cannot be committed by accident.
#
# NOT ignored, and must stay tracked:
#   nebula/device/spice/sky130_nfet_only.lib.spice  — OUR trimmed library (G36).
#   It contains only `.include` pointers into the out-of-tree PDK plus a header
#   and `.option scale=1.0u`; it redistributes no model cards.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
sky130A/
sky130_fd_pr/
sky130*/
libs.tech/
libs.ref/
open_pdks/
volare/
*.pm3.spice
*.corner.spice
!nebula/device/spice/sky130_nfet_only.lib.spice

